{
  "comment": "The steps of the realize program (generators/realize/), run in order by tools/generators/run.sh. Each step answers one decision spec of app/specs/realizability/spec.json over its whole request space (an each over the empty path stages the spec itself, compact): its witness pairs, live rules, totality and examples (RZ-01). A step reads repository files and the .gen/ outputs of this program's earlier steps only. Then each spec's outcomes and the values of its fields are gathered into .gen/rz-terms (one step per spec, each after the last), and rzcomp answers composition from them and the realizability model's reads: for every facet, how many of the fields that take another facet's outcomes say so, and each flaw in words (test/realize/composition.txt). Last, the settings: rzdrives lists which settings each facet of the coherence registry drives, rzsens which fields of each facet have a witness, rzbind answers one setting of the surface at a time (every field bound under it in the realizability model is a sensitive field of a facet the registry has it drive, and every such facet has a field bound), and rzset counts the settings bound and gives each flaw in words (test/realize/settings.txt). Last, the projection: rzroutes reads the root's facet table; rzmod reads every Prism module of app/src once (its judge of one request, its imports, its theorems and, where it has a judge, its request structure and constants) and rzpick keeps the short facts of those; rzmods and rzres say which module decides for each facet; and rzproj says, one deciding module at a time, how that module names the spec's fields, values and answers, or each fault in words (test/realize/projection.txt). Last, the descriptor: rzdirs lists the facets of the realizability model, rzcat gathers every fact this program wrote, and rzdesc says, one facet at a time, each reason the facet is refused in words, the number of its requests, the digest of its spec as staged (also in .gen/rz-terms, with whether it is rules or a tree), and its eleven elements as have and need (test/realize/descriptor.facts).",
